Independent implementation
--------------------------

This is not a fork. Every line here is written from scratch, from Clojure's
documented compilation semantics and Bazel's documented rule APIs.

Prior art exists and is worth naming, because ideas travel even when code does
not: simuons/rules_clojure and griffinbank/rules_clojure both solved parts of
this problem first, and this project owes them the shape of the question — how
Clojure's ahead-of-time compilation, which is transitive by default, can be made
to fit a build graph that wants one output per unit of source. The answers here
are arrived at independently and are deliberately structured differently: the
compiler runs as a dependency-free Java shim rather than as Clojure sharing a
classpath with user code, analysis runs in its own process instead of vendoring
the libraries it needs, dependency resolution goes through a checked-in lockfile
rather than a Clojure CLI download, and there is no persistent worker.

No code, documentation, comments or test fixtures are copied from either
project. Neither is affiliated with this one, and neither carries any copyright
in it.
